{"type":"text","timestamp":1787495588632,"sessionID":"ses_fd0f6a6f6ffeuCbicMa0SsYkFB","part":{"id":"prt_02f0a1b67001Eyo62LSSsffYdv","messageID":"msg_02f0a190d001QJhy3j82Q0Rxiu","sessionID":"ses_fd0f6a6f6ffeuCbicMa0SsYkFB","type":"text","text":"Implemented the benchmark run explorer in the four required files.\n\nSummary of changes:\n- `run-explorer.mjs`: kept the seeded `sampleRuns`, implemented `filterRuns`, `sortRuns`, and `summarizeRuns` without mutating inputs, and added browser-only rendering with safe DOM APIs.\n- `index.html`: semantic layout with intro, labeled filters, sort select, reset button, summary values, aria-live status, results list, and hidden empty state.\n- `styles.css`: responsive design with focus-visible, hover states, outcome badges, reduced-motion rule, and a 720 px breakpoint.\n- `student-tests.mjs`: two edge-case tests—zeroed summary for an empty array, and `cost-asc` sorting with known costs before `null` plus tie-breakers.\n\nAdded edge cases in student tests:\n1. Empty runs produce a fully zeroed summary.\n2. `cost-asc` sorts known numeric costs first, then falls back to score-desc and id for ties; null costs sort after known costs.\n\nTest result: 6/6 passing.\n\nBrowser behavior I could not directly verify:\n- Actual select change and reset interactions in a browser (only tested the pure functions via Node.js).\n- Visual rendering, color contrast, and responsive reflow across real viewports.\n- Keyboard focus-visible styling and reduced-motion behavior in a live browser.","time":{"start":1787495586663,"end":1787495588629}}}
